From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tseng <tseng.jayj@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:00:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] consensus: quarantine inherited Monero trust anchors

A fork of Monero inherits more than code. It inherits Monero's decisions about
what to TRUST: a fixed proof-of-work answer for one historical block, a
substituted id for another, hard-coded checkpoint hashes, a precompiled
checkpoint blob, and DNS names that hand out more checkpoints. Each is correct
for Monero and wrong for a different chain, and together they let a MeepCoin node
treat Monero's history as authoritative -- including rejecting its own valid
low-height blocks.

Each was witnessed live before removal, via the new standalone test:

  * height 202612 long hash: two materially different hashing blobs BOTH returned
    the inherited constant 84f64766...03000000 rather than their own MeepHash
    results (7c1abd90... for the first). The block's proof-of-work was literally
    unfalsifiable: any blob, any nonce, same answer. The main chain also disagreed
    with the alt chain, which already went straight to MeepHash.
  * built-in checkpoints: MAINNET 63, TESTNET 4, STAGENET 3 -- including Monero's
    height-1 and height-202612 ids and both foreign genesis hashes.
  * PER_BLOCK_CHECKPOINT was defined in the canonical build, compiling the 463,364
    byte Monero src/blocks/checkpoints.dat into the daemon.
  * load_checkpoints_from_dns was callable and returned success.

The corrections:

  cryptonote_tx_utils.cpp   remove the fixed height-202612 long hash. Every height
                            and every block version derives from the supplied
                            hashing blob through MeepHash-W v2. No replacement
                            exception; no MeepHash parameter changed.
  cryptonote_format_utils.cpp  remove the historical block-id substitution from
                            calculate_block_hash, including its second branch that
                            could return null_hash/false. A block id is derived
                            from the block. No MeepCoin constant replaces it.
  checkpoints.cpp           MAINNET/TESTNET/STAGENET default checkpoint sets are
                            EMPTY (70 ADD_CHECKPOINT2 entries removed) until
                            MeepCoin checkpoints are generated from MeepCoin's own
                            chain and separately reviewed. Copying Monero's values
                            or inventing replacements would each be a way of
                            pretending to have a reviewed answer.
  checkpoints.cpp           load_checkpoints_from_dns is structurally disabled and
                            the MoneroPulse domains are deleted, not merely unused.
                            It returns FALSE, not the inherited "return true".
  blockchain.cpp            the DNS acquisition path is gone entirely rather than
                            conditioned on a flag.
  cryptonote_core.cpp       --enforce-dns-checkpointing is REFUSED at argument
                            validation. Silently ignoring a flag whose purpose is
                            to enforce checkpoints would leave an operator
                            believing a protection is on when it is not.
  CMakeLists.txt            PER_BLOCK_CHECKPOINT forced off, and a cache value
                            asking for it is a FATAL_ERROR naming the removed blob
                            rather than a silent re-enable.
  src/blocks/checkpoints.dat  deleted, so there is nothing to compile even if the
                            option were somehow turned on.

NOT removed: BlockchainDB::fixup(). Its entire body is gated on the height-0 block
hash equalling Monero's mainnet genesis 418015bb...32e3. The test generates all
three MeepCoin genesis blocks and shows their ids (5ee18340..., 871bc633...,
825a2f71...) differ, so the guard can never match and the inherited body is
unreachable rather than merely unused. blockchain_db.cpp is byte-unchanged.

Tests, in the repository's existing standalone style (the pinned build sets
BUILD_TESTS=OFF, so anything added under tests/unit_tests would never run -- same
reasoning as meepcoin_hardfork_test.cpp):

  meepcoin_trust_anchor_test.cpp    66 passed, 0 failed (1.4 s)
  meepcoin_trust_anchor_guards.sh   24 passed, 0 failed (7 s)

The guards cover what a running binary cannot: the block-id remap only fired for a
block whose blob hashed to one exact Monero value, and constructing that preimage
is impractical, so the guard is that the constants are gone from the consensus
path. They also verify the CMake refusal for real, that MeepHash-W v2 sources are
byte-identical, and that genesis, emission, difficulty, hardfork schedule, wallet,
address and port sources are untouched by this commit.

Deliberately still inherited, and a separate later phase: Monero update/download
trust endpoints, general DNS probes, seed nodes, blocklists, and network branding.
No daemon, miner, P2P, wallet or network process was run. No genesis, emission,
difficulty, timestamp, hash-algorithm, address or economic change.

